    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is upheld in full. Under POL-NS-01 limb (c) the driver must hold position inside the pickup geofence for a continuous 300 seconds for a LARGE_VENUE pickup, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix (17:15:00), not from the 'arrived' tap. The GPS trace EV-GPS-09103 measures a single continuous in-geofence hold of 240 seconds, from 17:15:00 to 17:19:00 — a shortfall of 60 seconds against the 300-second minimum — and the trip record EV-TRIP-09103 agrees, showing arrival at 17:15:20 and driver cancellation at 17:19:00. POL-NS-06 makes this strict liability: where the effective dwell falls below the minimum the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present or responsive. The SGD 8.00 charged on EV-FARE-09103 is therefore refunded in full. No accumulation of separate intervals under POL-NS-06(i) is available: the trace shows exactly one in-geofence interval (run_count 1), so there is no second interval to sum, and the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09103-01 is MISSING (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0), so limb (i) has nothing to operate on in any event. To the driver: the tribunal accepts everything you established. Arrival under POL-NS-02 is made out — the trace places you about 24 m from the pin, well inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius, and the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event. There is no false arrival marker under POL-NS-05 (stationary, 0.0 km/h, at 24 m, no gap, no excursion). The amount reconciles with the fee schedule, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged: the SGD 8.00 line is the greater of the SGD 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the SGD 8.00 RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee, exactly as the resolution rule requires. No anti-farming pattern exists under POL-NS-07: no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against completed_trips_30d of 120, a rate of 0.008, below both the absolute and the rate threshold. None of this changes the result: POL-NS-07 pays compensation only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and limb (c) is not satisfied, so the driver receives no compensation. This is a 60-second timing shortfall, not a finding of driver misconduct, and it carries no adverse referral or escalation. The rider's other routes are not needed but are noted: POL-NS-04 cannot be run — the chat log EV-CHAT-09103 contains no rider message and the rider's track sits about 519 m from the pin with zero qualifying fixes — but the refund does not depend on it, because POL-NS-06 conditions the refund on the driver's dwell alone. POL-NS-05 does not bite in either direction. On escalation, no POL-NS-09 trigger fires: both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, the POL-NS-07 check does not trip, and the deciding fact — the dwell — is carried by a COMPLETE artifact at weight 1.0 (EV-GPS-09103, corroborated by EV-TRIP-09103), with no POL-NS-08(a)-(d) impairment: no clock skew (the 'arrived' event at 17:15:20 sits on a 10-second GPS cadence), 25 fixes with a 0-second maximum gap across the window, 3 chat messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count, and a reconciled fare. The confidence cap is 1.0, the minimum weight among the artifacts carrying the deciding fact, so confidence of 0.95 stands above the 0.70 floor and the case is decided now rather than held."
